WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:05.989
Gem was locking a display case at Gem's Jewelry.

2
00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:11.069
An old woman approached the case.

3
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.152
She wore a black cape and a pointy black hat.

4
00:00:14.153 --> 00:00:17.751
She carried a large sack.

5
00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:22.202
Gem smiled. "Can I show you some jewelry?"

6
00:00:22.203 --> 00:00:27.731
"No, thanks. I'm just looking around," the old woman said.

7
00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:33.699
She reached into her sack. "Would you like some candy?"

8
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.034
"Sure." Gem took a small chocolate. "Thank you."

9
00:00:38.035 --> 00:00:39.800
Gem put away her key.

10
00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:43.077
She turned around when she heard the bell over the door jingle.

11
00:00:43.078 --> 00:00:45.777
When she turned back, the old woman was gone.

12
00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:48.541
Gem stared in horror at the display case.

13
00:00:48.542 --> 00:00:51.459
All of the precious jewelry inside was gone too.

14
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:56.323
In its place were pieces of candy!

15
00:00:56.324 --> 00:01:00.077
Gem ran outside. "Stop, thief!"

16
00:01:00.078 --> 00:01:02.901
The witch dashed around the corner and hid.

17
00:01:02.902 --> 00:01:06.964
She opened her sack. Now it was full of jewelry.

18
00:01:06.965 --> 00:01:11.010
The witch cackled loudly.

19
00:01:11.011 --> 00:01:16.992
"Soon I'll be rich—and much more powerful!"

20
00:01:16.993 --> 00:01:20.950
"I read five books this month," Terrell said.

21
00:01:20.951 --> 00:01:23.558
He put five tickets in a pile on the table.

22
00:01:23.559 --> 00:01:28.665
"Me too," Mara said. "We have ten tickets now."

23
00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:31.189
Roxy and her friends were in the school library.

24
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.848
The school was having a reading marathon this month.

25
00:01:33.849 --> 00:01:36.846
Students earned a ticket for each book they read.

26
00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:44.047
Jack added his tickets to the pile. "I read two books."

27
00:01:44.048 --> 00:01:48.279
"Sorry, guys." Roxy added one ticket to the pile.

28
00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.028
"I love reading. But I was super busy this month.

29
00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:55.542
Whenever I wanted to read, something pulled me away."

30
00:01:55.543 --> 00:01:58.280
"No problem, Roxy," Terrell said quickly.

31
00:01:58.281 --> 00:02:03.035
"We've got 13 tickets. That's enough for us to get a pretty good prize."

32
00:02:03.036 --> 00:02:05.887
The friends looked at the list of prizes.

33
00:02:05.888 --> 00:02:09.044
"Let's get the pirate hats," Jack said.

34
00:02:09.045 --> 00:02:13.537
"We only have enough tickets for one hat," Roxy said.

35
00:02:13.538 --> 00:02:17.702
"What about the spooky stickers?" Mara said.

36
00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:21.095
"There are ghosts and monsters," Jack said.

37
00:02:21.096 --> 00:02:25.405
"We could share them," Terrell said. "What do you think, Roxy?"

38
00:02:25.406 --> 00:02:29.895
"Um . . ." Just then Roxy's watch beeped.

39
00:02:29.896 --> 00:02:33.423
"Oh, I, uh, just remembered something!

40
00:02:33.424 --> 00:02:38.917
There's a book I want to read on that shelf!"

41
00:02:38.918 --> 00:02:42.326
Roxy darted behind a bookcase.

42
00:02:42.327 --> 00:02:45.426
"Hello, Mayor Bloom," she whispered.

43
00:02:45.427 --> 00:02:49.481
"Why are you whispering, Rocket Girl?" the mayor asked.

44
00:02:49.482 --> 00:02:53.074
"I'm in the library. What's wrong?"

45
00:02:53.075 --> 00:02:58.450
"A thief just stole some precious jewelry from Gem's," Mayor Bloom said.

46
00:02:58.451 --> 00:03:01.022
"And it's a strange situation.

47
00:03:01.023 --> 00:03:05.054
She stole the jewelry without opening the display case.

48
00:03:05.055 --> 00:03:07.945
We have no idea how she did it!"

49
00:03:07.946 --> 00:03:16.039
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy whispered. "I'm on my way!"

